name: sovereign-swarm
description: |
  Sovereign Swarm integration - routes all queries through the Intent Gate
  for domain-specific specialist reasoning. Makes the Swarm the brain of Hermes.

version: 2.2.0
author: Sovereign Swarm
icon: 🧠

hooks:
  pre_process:
    command: python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/pre_process.py
    input: query
    output: json

config:
  intent_gate_model: {{DISTILL_MODEL}}
  distill_model: {{DISTILL_MODEL}}
  reasoning_model: {{REASONING_MODEL}}

specialists:
{{SPECIALISTS}}

documentation: |
  ## Sovereign Swarm Skill v2.2

  Four-tier pipeline that processes EVERY query automatically.
  Resilience features: health check, fallback chains, circuit breaker,
  logging, metrics, caching, validation, hard timeout.

  ### Tier 1: Intent Gate (Automatic Pre-Hook)
  - Script: ~/.hermes/scripts/pre_process.py
  - Model: None — keyword-based classification with word-boundary matching
  - Reads: ONLY the current message — NO conversation history
  - Output: Domain tag ({{DOMAIN_LIST}})
  - Time: ~0 seconds (no model call)

  ### Tier 2: Distill
  - Script: ~/.hermes/scripts/pre_process.py
  - Model: {{DISTILL_MODEL}}
  - Fallback: {{DISTILL_MODEL}} → gpt-oss:20b-cloud → gemma4:12b (local) → original text
  - Strips filler words, restructures into short active-voice sentences
  - One fact per sentence. No idioms. No filler.
  - Token savings: ~200 tokens → ~60 tokens per message

  ### Tier 3: Evaluator Gate
  - Script: ~/.hermes/scripts/pre_process.py
  - Model: {{DISTILL_MODEL}} (same as distill)
  - Fallback: {{DISTILL_MODEL}} → gpt-oss:20b-cloud → gemma4:12b (local) → pass to heavy model
  - After distilling, asks: "Can you answer this confidently without tools, research, or live data?"
  - If YES: Returns answer directly. Heavy model NEVER called. Saves ~$0.02/query.
  - If NO: Passes through to Tier 4 as normal.
  - Skipped for FULL intensity queries (research, analyze, draft, motion, brief)
  - Only answers: simple facts, definitions, common knowledge, simple math
  - Declines: legal research, live data, system-specific questions, tool-dependent queries

  ### Tier 4: Heavy Reasoning
  - Model: {{REASONING_MODEL}}
  - Receives: clean, classified input (~60 tokens)
  - Never sees: original verbose input or full conversation history
  - Token savings: 99.7% reduction (20,200 → 60 tokens)

  ### Resilience Features
  - Health check: fast-fail (3s) if Ollama is down
  - Fallback chains: cloud → local → tiny local → original text
  - Circuit breaker: 3 strikes, 5-min cooldown, persists to disk
  - Logging: every decision to ~/.hermes/logs/pipeline.log
  - Metrics: view with `python3 ~/.hermes/scripts/pipeline_metrics.py`
  - Caching: LRU cache (100 entries) for repeated queries
  - Input/output validation with safe fallbacks
  - Hard timeout: 15-second kill switch
  - Word-boundary keyword matching prevents false positives

  ### How it works
  1. User sends message
  2. Pre-process hook fires automatically — health check runs
  3. Intent Gate classifies domain via word-boundary keyword matching
  4. Distill strips filler from input (with fallback chain)
  5. Evaluator decides if it can answer (with fallback chain)
  6. If evaluator answers: response returned directly
  7. If evaluator passes: heavy model receives clean, classified input
  8. All steps logged with timestamps and latency
